ti ! (et si tu es parti déjà fatigué(e) à cause de l'entraînement fractionné de la veille par exemple... alors tu ne devrais pas être plus fatigué(e) encore en rentrant sinon mieux vaut raccourcir le footing avant de rentrer dans cet état d'accumulation de fatigue supplémentaire!)","test":false,"importance":false,"trainingType":"EF","trainingCategory":"road_basic_endurance","exercisesBlocks":[{"repeat":1,"exercises":[{"_t":"SmartExercise","name":"EF_40","exerciseType":"running","pace":{"name":"EF","value":328,"kind":"range","zoneKind":"Z2","abstract":false,"slug":"ef"},"durations":[{"value":40,"timeUnit":"minutes"}],"manualLap":false}]}],"difficulty":1,"trainingIndex":1,"weekDate":1786320000000,"status":"todo","stats":{"_t":"SessionExpectedStats","expectedDistance":6.997084548104956,"expectedDuration":2400},"paceZones":[{"kind":"Z2","duration":2400,"pace":{"value":328}}]},{"_t":"SmartSessionWithStats","sport":"road","name":"S60_600_2","description":"Séance de seuil 60' où tu vas enchaîner **5 répétitions de 4'** à l'allure cible entrecoupées de 2' de footing lent pour récupérer.","displayName":"Seuil 60","coachAdvice":"L'erreur serait de laisser la fatigue prendre le dessus sur ton efficacité. Plus la séance avance, plus tu fatigues. Plus tu fatigues moins tu fais attention à ta posture, ton souffle, ton gainage. Cela double la fatigue ! Donc concentre-toi sur tous tes intervalles et ne dégrade pas ta technique.","test":false,"importance":true,"trainingType":"Intensity","trainingCategory":"road_intensity","exercisesBlocks":[{"repeat":1,"exercises":[{"_t":"SmartExercise","name":"WU_15","exerciseType":"warm-up","pace":{"name":"EF","value":328,"kind":"range","zoneKind":"Z2","abstract":false,"slug":"ef"},"durations":[{"value":15,"timeUnit":"minutes"}],"manualLap":true}],"blockType":"warm-up"},{"repeat":5,"exercises":[{"_t":"SmartExercise","name":"S60_4","exerciseType":"running","pace":{"name":"Seuil 60","value":255,"kind":"single-value","zoneKind":"Z4","abstract":false,